    <article class="ba-body">
      <p>Every dietary supplement sold in the U.S. carries information the FDA requires. Knowing what to look for makes it easier to compare products.</p>
      <h2 id="highlights">Highlights</h2><ul class="ba-hl"><li>Check the ingredient list — ours has exactly one ingredient.</li><li>Look at the serving size and servings per container.</li><li>The asterisk links to the FDA disclaimer for structure/function statements.</li></ul>
      <h2 id="s0">Ingredients first</h2><p>A single-ingredient powder should list just one botanical, with its Latin name. No fillers, flow agents or added sugars.</p><h2 id="s1">Serving size & nutrition</h2><p>Our pouches list serving size (2 rounded teaspoons), servings per container (38–45) and a nutrition panel.</p><h2 id="s2">The asterisk</h2><p>Statements such as “traditionally used to support…” must carry the disclaimer: these statements have not been evaluated by the FDA; the product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any disease.</p>
      
      <div class="art-prod"><img src="{{ 'pouch-amla.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Amla Powder pouch" width="620" height="861" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div><span class="jr-meta">Featured in this article</span><h3>Amla Powder</h3><p>Traditionally used to support immunity, digestion, and radiant skin & hair.*</p><div class="hero-ctas"><button class="btn sm" type="button" data-add="amla">Add — {{ all_products['amla-powder'].price | money }}</button><a class="btn ghost sm" href="/products/amla-powder">View product</a></div></div></div>
      <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2><details class="ba-faq"><summary>Why do you list batch and expiry dates?</summary><p>So every pouch can be traced back to its production batch.</p></details><details class="ba-faq"><summary>What does the asterisk on a supplement label mean?</summary><p>It points to the FDA disclaimer that statements such as “traditionally used to support…” have not been evaluated by the FDA and that the product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any disease.</p></details><details class="ba-faq"><summary>What should a single-ingredient powder list as ingredients?</summary><p>Just one botanical, with its Latin name — no fillers, flow agents or added sugars.</p></details>
      <h2 id="refs">References</h2><ol class="ba-refs"><li><a href="https://www.fda.gov/food/dietary-supplements-guidance-documents-regulatory-information/dietary-supplement-labeling-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dietary Supplement Labeling Guide — U.S. FDA</a></li><li><a href="https://www.fda.gov/food/dietary-supplements" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dietary Supplements — U.S. Food & Drug Administration</a></li></ol>
